   "text": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants a Rust function that parses a CSV line into fields, handling quoted commas (i.e., fields that are enclosed in quotes and may contain commas within them). They also want unit tests.\n\nLet me think about what a proper CSV parser needs to handle:\n1. Simple fields: `a,b,c` \u2192 [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]\n2. Quoted fields with commas: `\"hello, world\",b,c` \u2192 [\"hello, world\", \"b\", \"c\"]\n3. Quoted fields with escaped quotes: `\"He said \"\"hi\"\"\",b` \u2192 ['He said \"hi\"', \"b\"]\n4. Empty fields: `a,,c` \u2192 [\"a\", \"\", \"c\"]\n5. Quoted empty fields: `\"\"` \u2192 [\"\"]\n6. Whitespace handling (optional, but let's keep it simple - no trimming by default, or maybe trim)\n\nLet me design the function:\n\n```rust\nfn parse_csv_line(line: &str) -> Vec<String>\n```\n\nThe algorithm:\n- Iterate through characters\n- Track state: in_quotes or not\n- When we see a quote, toggle in_quotes\n- When we see a comma"
